.TH LINKAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
linkat \- Linux x86-64 syscall 265
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_260_299.h>
.B int linkat(int old_directory, const char* old_path, int new_directory, const char* new_path, int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a hard link relative to directory descriptors.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linkat (2)
